From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: let the ADSP sleep with audio open at suspend

A PCM left open at suspend - a game or a film still playing when the
power button is pressed - kept its AudioReach graph, and with it the
ADSP, awake for the whole sleep. Three changes from armada-os/armada
(commit 456a9af, their 0528 to 0530), combined:

- sc8280xp: suspend the card and its streams, so open PCMs are
  suspended with the system
- q6apm: fail a graph open when the DSP rejects it
- q6apm-dai, q6apm-lpass-dais: release the graphs across system
  suspend and restore them source-then-sink on resume; a port restored
  at resume is not stopped again by the first prepare

Measured there on an Odin 3: the extra sleep power with a sound playing
at suspend fell from 0.091 W to 0.003-0.007 W at the USB input.

One hunk is rebased onto our 0612. It moves the start-at-prepare into
q6apm_lpass_dai_configure(), which starts MI2S playback ports only, as
armada does; our 0612 started every playback port there. The speakers
are on PRIMARY_MI2S_RX, so their aw88166 still get BCLK before
PRE_PMU. Headphone (RX_CODEC_DMA) and DisplayPort ports start at the
trigger again, as upstream does.
